ARIF AND ORS . VS. ZULE KHAN PAGE NO. 10 OF 29 purpose; that the second election card is of village Shikrawa and all the details have been given by appellant no.1 in application u/s 340 Cr. P.C. filed by him in the present case which was also dismissed on 29.10.2018; that father of the respondent no.2 used the said both two I.D. cards as per his wishes and convenience; that the respondent no.2 was not residing in Delhi at the time of filing the complaint nor she was having any proof to show that she was residing at New Delhi and thus the Ld.
Trial Court has no territorial jurisdiction to entertain the petition under D.V. Act;
that the Ld. Trial Court has further erred in not noting that the respondent no.2 has miserably failed to prove the domestic violence against the appellants and on the other hand appellant no.1 produced copy of judgments vide which he has been acquitted in various cases filed by the respondent no.1 and her father and that the Ld.
Magistrate has wrongly mentioned in para No.21 of the order that mere registration of F.I.R. would not falsify the case of the complainant without realizing that he has been acquitted by the Ld. Trial Court as well as in some other cases by the appellate Court; that before 25.12.2013, there was no allegation of demand of dowry and harassment on account of the same which is clear from the above said judgments;

